.IX Title "OPENSSL-ECH 1ossl"
.TH OPENSSL-ECH 1ossl "2026-04-14" "4.0.0" "OpenSSL"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
openssl\-ech \- ECH key generation
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBopenssl\fR \fBech\fR
[\fB\-help\fR]
[\fB\-verbose\fR]
[\fB\-in\fR \fIfiles\fR]
[\fB\-out\fR \fIfile\fR]
[\fB\-public_name\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB\-max_name_len\fR \fIlen\fR]
[\fB\-suite\fR \fIsuite_str\fR]
[\fB\-ech_version\fR \fIversion\fR]
[\fB\-select\fR \fInumber\fR]
[\fB\-text\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
The \fIopenssl\-ech\fR\|(1) command generates Encrypted Client Hello (\s-1ECH\s0) key pairs
in the ECHConfig \s-1PEM\s0 file format as specified in
<https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc9934>.
.PP
That format consists of an optional private key in PKCS#8 format and a base64
encoded ECHConfigList containing an entry with a matching public value (and
possibly other entries as well).
.SH "OPTIONS"
.IX Header "OPTIONS"
The following options are supported:
.IP "\fB\-help\fR" 4
.IX Item "-help"
Print out a usage message.
.IP "\fB\-verbose\fR" 4
.IX Item "-verbose"
Print more verbosely.
.IP "\fB\-in\fR" 4
.IX Item "-in"
Provide an input \s-1ECH PEM\s0 file for printing or merging. Up to five
input files can be provided via use of multiple \fBin\fR arguments.
.IP "\fB\-out\fR \fIfile\fR" 4
.IX Item "-out file"
Name of output ECHConfig \s-1PEM\s0 file.  If a new key pair was generated the output
file will contain the private key and encoded ECHConfigList.  If one or more
input files was provided the output file will contain a set of ECHConfigList
values with public keys from the inputs, and no private key(s).
.IP "\fB\-text\fR" 4
.IX Item "-text"
Provide human-readable text output.
.IP "\fB\-public_name\fR \fIname\fR" 4
.IX Item "-public_name name"
The \s-1DNS\s0 name to use in the \*(L"public_name\*(R" field of the ECHConfig.
.IP "\fB\-max_name_len\fR \fInum\fR" 4
.IX Item "-max_name_len num"
Maximum name length field value to use in the ECHConfig.
.IP "\fB\-suite\fR \fIstr\fR" 4
.IX Item "-suite str"
\&\s-1HPKE\s0 suite to use in the ECHConfig.
.IP "\fB\-ech_version\fR \fIversion\fR" 4
.IX Item "-ech_version version"
The \s-1ECH\s0 version to use in the ECHConfig. Only 0xfe0d is supported in this version.
.IP "\fB\-select\fR \fInumber\fR" 4
.IX Item "-select number"
Select the N\-th ECHConfig/public key from the set of input \s-1ECH PEM\s0 files and output
that.
.SH "NOTES"
.IX Header "NOTES"
Ciphersuites are specified using a comma-separated list of IANA-registered
codes/numbers e.g. \*(L"\-c 0x20,1,3\*(R" or a comma-separated list of strings from:
\&\- KEMs: p256, p384, p521, x25519, x448
\&\- KDFs: hkdf\-sha256, hkdf\-sha384, hkdf\-sha512
\&\- AEADs: aes128gcm, aes256gcm, chachapoly1305
.PP
For example the default is: x25519, hkdf\-sha256, aes128gcm
See \fIOSSL_HPKE_CTX_new\fR\|(3) for details.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fIopenssl\fR\|(1),
\&\fIopenssl\-s_client\fR\|(1),
\&\fIopenssl\-s_server\fR\|(1),
\&\fISSL_set1_echstore\fR\|(3)
.SH "HISTORY"
.IX Header "HISTORY"
This functionality described here was added in OpenSSL 4.0.
